/* PayHub Merchant — English strings.

   Two key styles coexist:

     1. Structured keys (`payment.detail.title`) used by `NSLocalizedString` and
        explicit `LocalizedStringKey("…")` lookups in newer files. Entries here
        are not strictly required — the call sites pass an English `value:`
        fallback — but populating them keeps EN + AR in lock-step and gives
        translation tools one place to look.

     2. English-literal keys (`"Pay-links" = "Pay-links";`) used wherever a view
        has an inline `Text("Pay-links")`. SwiftUI interprets a string literal
        as a `LocalizedStringKey`, so the key IS the English text — the AR file
        translates them. The pre-D7.1 scaffold leans on this style for most
        chrome strings; keep it working unchanged.
*/

